---
/**
 * The problem, in one picture: what was agreed stays put, the code walks away,
 * and every mechanical gate keeps saying yes the whole time.
 */
---

<figure class="drift" data-anim>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="drift-t drift-d">
    <title id="drift-t">Architectural drift over six weeks</title>
    <desc id="drift-d">
      The recorded decision holds a straight line while the codebase curves away from
      it. The compiler and the test suite keep passing throughout; only the question
      "is this what we agreed?" comes back false.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <linearGradient id="gapFill" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--fail)" stop-opacity="0.32" />
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--fail)" stop-opacity="0.03" />
      </linearGradient>
      <linearGradient id="codeStroke" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
        <stop offset="0%" stop-color="var(--fg-muted)" />
        <stop offset="55%" stop-color="var(--clay)" />
        <stop offset="100%" stop-color="var(--fail)" />
      </linearGradient>
    </defs>

    <!-- time axis -->
    <line class="axis" x1="70" y1="300" x2="700" y2="300" />
    {
      [
        [70, 'day one'],
        [290, 'week two'],
        [510, 'week four'],
        [690, 'week six'],
      ].map(([x, label]) => (
        <g class="tick">
          <line x1={x} y1="295" x2={x} y2="305" />
          <text x={x} y="324" text-anchor={x === 70 ? 'start' : x === 690 ? 'end' : 'middle'}>
            {label}
          </text>
        </g>
      ))
    }

    <!-- the widening gap between intent and code -->
    <path
      class="gap"
      d="M70 120 H700 V232 C560 232 400 160 240 122 C180 110 120 118 70 120 Z"
      fill="url(#gapFill)"
    />

    <!-- what was agreed: a straight line that does not move -->
    <line class="agreed" x1="70" y1="120" x2="700" y2="120" />
    <g class="label label--agreed">
      <text x="70" y="102">what we agreed</text>
      <text class="sub" x="70" y="86">.jasper/decisions/001-boundaries.yaml</text>
    </g>

    <!-- what the code actually did -->
    <path
      class="code"
      d="M70 120 C120 118 180 110 240 122 C400 160 560 232 700 232"
      fill="none"
      stroke="url(#codeStroke)"
    />
    <circle class="head" r="6" cx="700" cy="232" />
    <g class="label label--code">
      <text x="700" y="262" text-anchor="end">what the code does</text>
    </g>

    <!-- commits along the way: each one individually reasonable -->
    {
      [
        [240, 122],
        [370, 152],
        [480, 190],
        [590, 214],
      ].map(([cx, cy], i) => (
        <circle class="commit" cx={cx} cy={cy} r="4" style={`--i:${i}`} />
      ))
    }

    <!-- the verdicts -->
    <g class="verdicts">
      <g class="verdict v-ok" style="--i:0">
        <rect x="72" y="18" width="150" height="34" rx="17" />
        <text x="95" y="40">compiler</text>
        <text class="mark ok" x="200" y="41">✓</text>
      </g>
      <g class="verdict v-ok" style="--i:1">
        <rect x="236" y="18" width="150" height="34" rx="17" />
        <text x="259" y="40">test suite</text>
        <text class="mark ok" x="364" y="41">✓</text>
      </g>
      <g class="verdict v-bad" style="--i:2">
        <rect x="400" y="18" width="190" height="34" rx="17" />
        <text x="423" y="40">is this what we agreed?</text>
        <text class="mark bad" x="568" y="41">✗</text>
      </g>
    </g>

    <!-- the callout -->
    <g class="drift-tag">
      <line x1="470" y1="124" x2="470" y2="187" />
      <text x="482" y="160">drift</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <figcaption>
    Every commit on that curve compiled, passed review and passed CI. Drift is, by
    definition, made of changes that nothing mechanical objects to.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .drift {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .drift svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .axis {
    stroke: var(--line);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .tick line {
    stroke: var(--line-strong);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .tick text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--fg-faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  /* --- the agreed line: drawn first, then holds ------------------------- */
  .agreed {
    stroke: var(--amber);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 7 6;
    stroke-dashoffset: 660;
    animation: draw-agreed 0.9s var(--ease-io) forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }
  @keyframes draw-agreed {
    to {
      stroke-dashoffset: 0;
    }
  }

  .label text {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 550;
    fill: var(--fg);
  }
  .label .sub {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 400;
    fill: var(--fg-faint);
  }
  .label {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fade 0.5s var(--ease) forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }
  .label--agreed {
    animation-delay: 0.5s;
  }
  .label--code {
    animation-delay: 2.5s;
  }

  /* --- the code path: drawn slowly, pulling away ------------------------ */
  .code {
    stroke-width: 2.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-dasharray: 700;
    stroke-dashoffset: 700;
    animation: draw-code 2.2s var(--ease-io) 0.75s forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }
  @keyframes draw-code {
    to {
      stroke-dashoffset: 0;
    }
  }

  .head {
    fill: var(--fail);
    opacity: 0;
    animation: pop 0.5s var(--ease) 2.7s forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }

  .commit {
    fill: var(--bg);
    stroke: var(--clay);
    stroke-width: 2;
    opacity: 0;
    animation: pop 0.45s var(--ease) forwards;
    animation-delay: calc(1.1s + var(--i) * 0.42s);
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }

  .gap {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fade 0.9s var(--ease) 2.3s forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }

  /* --- verdict pills ----------------------------------------------------- */
  .verdict rect {
    fill: var(--surface);
    stroke: var(--line);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .verdict text {
    font-size: 13px;
    fill: var(--fg-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .verdict .mark {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .verdict .ok {
    fill: var(--pass);
  }
  .verdict .bad {
    fill: var(--fail);
  }
  .v-bad rect {
    stroke: color-mix(in oklab, var(--fail) 55%, var(--line));
    fill: color-mix(in oklab, var(--fail) 9%, var(--surface));
  }
  .v-bad text {
    fill: var(--fg);
  }

  .verdict {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-8px);
    animation: rise 0.55s var(--ease) forwards;
    animation-delay: calc(3s + var(--i) * 0.22s);
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }

  .drift-tag {
    opacity: 0;
    animation: fade 0.6s var(--ease) 2.8s forwards;
    animation-play-state: var(--run, paused);
  }
  .drift-tag line {
    stroke: var(--fail);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
  }
  .drift-tag text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--fail);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  @keyframes fade {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }
  @keyframes pop {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(0.3);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: scale(1);
    }
  }
  @keyframes rise {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .commit,
  .head {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: center;
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .verdict text {
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .tick text {
      font-size: 13px;
    }
  }
</style>
